---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import GravitySceneMount from '../components/hero/GravitySceneMount.astro';
---

<Layout title="Identity Engineering">
	<main>
		<!-- Hero: Identity Stem -->
		<section class="relative flex flex-col min-h-[100dvh] bg-[#0a0a0f]">
			<div class="shrink-0 z-10 text-center max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 w-full pt-24 md:pt-28 pb-3 md:pb-4">
				<h1 class="text-6xl sm:text-7xl md:text-[5.5rem] lg:text-[6.5rem] font-bold tracking-tighter leading-[0.9] mb-4 md:mb-5 text-white">
					Identity Engineering
				</h1>
				<p class="text-lg md:text-xl lg:text-2xl text-white/50 max-w-2xl mx-auto font-light">
					A science-inspired framework for shaping conscious identities in the AI era.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="relative flex-1 min-h-[52dvh] w-full">
				<GravitySceneMount />
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Why: necessity + two forces -->
		<section class="py-28 md:py-36 border-t border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">Why</div>
				<h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-8 text-white leading-[1.1]">
					This approach answers a necessity.
				</h2>
				<div class="mb-8 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
						This framework serves systems-thinking individuals and teams with enough decision latitude to make consequential identity choices.
						It is intentionally scoped and does not claim universal applicability.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="space-y-6 text-lg text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
					<p>
						We built much of modern human identity on intelligence.
						It is what many of us take ourselves to be: the one who knows, reasons, writes, decides, invents.
						For large parts of the high-wage economy that self-image is also the job description.
						Knowledge work is often cited around <strong class="text-white/80">two fifths of the workforce</strong> in advanced economies; for those roles the computer is usually the main tool.
					</p>
					<p>
						Artificial intelligence is now exceeding human performance in more and more cognitive domains.
						That creates an economic question: why pay a human wage for work a machine does better and cheaper?
						And a social question: what do we do when “who we are” is no longer primarily knowledge work?
					</p>

					<div class="my-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
						<div class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6">
							<div class="mb-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-400/70">Force 1 · Identity</div>
							<p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-white/70">
								Latin <em class="text-white/90 not-italic">identitas</em> means <strong class="text-white/90">sameness</strong>: the best possible recognizability of a self across time. Who we are, as something that can still be the same after change.
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="rounded-2xl border border-violet-400/20 bg-violet-400/[0.04] p-6">
							<div class="mb-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-violet-400/70">Force 2 · Intelligence</div>
							<p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-white/70">
								Intelligence, in the reading Identity Engineering adopts, is the capacity to keep and expand <strong class="text-white/90">future freedom of action</strong>. This directional claim is supported by several independent lines of work (causal entropic forces, empowerment, active inference, predictive processing). None is treated as a derived physical law of identity. The shared direction is taken as a normative design goal. See <a href="/blog/causal-entropy-as-design-telos" class="text-white/90 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-white/50 transition">multi-source grounding</a>.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<p>
						When intelligence scales exponentially, those two pulls no longer sit quietly side by side.
						They start to feel like opposing forces:
					</p>
					<ul class="space-y-3 pl-1">
						<li class="flex gap-3">
							<span class="text-violet-400 shrink-0">→</span>
							<span>
								<strong class="text-white/80">Intelligence</strong> pulls toward a maximally free, open, diverse future: more paths, less fixed form.
							</span>
						</li>
						<li class="flex gap-3">
							<span class="text-cyan-400 shrink-0">←</span>
							<span>
								<strong class="text-white/80">Identity</strong> pulls toward the best possible recognizability of the self: still us, still continuous, still owned.
							</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						Today we often recognize ourselves in the work we spent years building.
						Finding an alternative is not a casual rebrand when the market stops pricing our known activity
						at a human wage. Pure sameness freezes. Pure option-maximization dissolves.
						The live problem is the tension between them.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong class="text-white/80">Identity Engineering</strong> exists to address exactly that tension: how to keep a self recognizable while intelligence (human and artificial) multiplies future freedom, and how to turn that into practical application. <a href="/foundations" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 hover:text-white hover:decoration-white/50 transition">Foundations →</a>
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Framework overview: three scales, two lenses -->
		<section class="py-28 md:py-36 border-t border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">Framework</div>
				<h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-6 text-white leading-[1.1] max-w-3xl">
					Single. Interactive. Collective.
				</h2>
				<p class="text-lg text-white/50 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-16">
					Three scales only, under two lenses: physics geometry and living form.
					The OS is how that map is used. It is not a fourth scale.
				</p>

				<div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-6">
					<div class="border-t border-white/15 pt-8">
						<div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/35 mb-4">01 · Single</div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">One identity</h3>
						<p class="text-white/50 leading-relaxed text-base mb-4">
							<strong class="text-white/70">Time</strong> (Identity Stem); <strong class="text-white/70">Mass</strong>, <strong class="text-white/70">Curvature</strong>, <strong class="text-white/70">Rotation</strong>.
						</p>
						<p class="text-sm text-white/35 leading-relaxed">
							Internal geometry and stability. Biology: Gene, Boundary, Cell, Metabolism.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="border-t border-white/15 pt-8">
						<div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/35 mb-4">02 · Interactive</div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">Between identities</h3>
						<p class="text-white/50 leading-relaxed text-base mb-4">
							<strong class="text-white/70">Gravitation</strong>, <strong class="text-white/70">Relativity</strong>, <strong class="text-white/70">Frequency</strong>.
						</p>
						<p class="text-sm text-white/35 leading-relaxed">
							Forces and relation in a field of others. Biology: Signal, Recognition, Coupling.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="border-t border-white/15 pt-8">
						<div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/35 mb-4">03 · Collective</div>
						<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">Emergent whole</h3>
						<p class="text-white/50 leading-relaxed text-base mb-4">
							<strong class="text-white/70">Emergence</strong> and <strong class="text-white/70">Damping</strong>.
						</p>
						<p class="text-sm text-white/35 leading-relaxed">
							Higher-order coherence under stress. Biology: Multicellularity, Specialization, Regulation.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="mt-14 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
					<a
						href="/framework"
						class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-8 py-3.5 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition"
					>Explore the Framework
						<span class="text-black/50">→</span></a>
					<a
						href="/os"
						class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-8 py-3.5 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/80 hover:bg-white/5 hover:text-white transition"
					>OS: make it usable
						<span class="text-white/40">→</span></a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Architect shift -->
		<section class="py-24 border-t border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8 text-center">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">Shift</div>
				<p class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight text-white/90 leading-snug">
					Executor → Author → Architect
				</p>
				<p class="mt-6 text-lg text-white/45 leading-relaxed max-w-xl mx-auto">
					Not only shape our own stems. Build language and structures others can use
					to make differentials transparent and vision gradients sharp.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Big Questions teaser -->
		<section class="py-28 md:py-36 border-t border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">Frontier</div>
				<h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-8 text-white leading-[1.1]">
					The map is incomplete on purpose.
				</h2>
				<p class="text-lg text-white/55 leading-relaxed mb-6">
					The framework is grounded in human-scale identity across three scales: time, mass, curvature, rotation,
					gravitation, relativity, frequency, emergence, and damping, read also as living form under the biology lens.
					That foundation is necessary, not sufficient for every future already becoming plausible.
				</p>
				<p class="text-lg text-white/55 leading-relaxed mb-12">
					Substrate independence, collective scale, AI co-identity, and more:
					questions that cannot yet be fully answered, but must already be asked.
				</p>
				<a
					href="/big-questions"
					class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-8 py-3.5 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/80 hover:bg-white/5 hover:text-white transition"
				>Big Questions
					<span class="text-white/40">→</span></a>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Close -->
		<section class="py-24 border-t border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8 text-center">
				<p class="text-xl text-white/50 mb-10 max-w-lg mx-auto">
					The framework is open. Start with the geometry or the OS.
				</p>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 justify-center">
					<a href="/framework" class="px-8 py-3.5 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition">Framework</a>
					<a href="/os" class="px-8 py-3.5 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">OS</a>
					<a href="/big-questions" class="px-8 py-3.5 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Big Questions</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
